-- title:
--   Separating a place from its level translate by a chart function
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and a field $FSS$ that is an algebra over the residue field of $A$. Let $\bar F =$ `fieldBar q M'` be the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, inside Laurent series, of the function field of the modular curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $\bar F$ with reduced field $FSS$: a valuation subring `R.integers` of $\bar F$ meeting the constants exactly in $A$, together with a surjective homomorphism `R.residue` onto $FSS$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction on $A$, and such that every nonzero element of $\bar F$ has a constant multiple that is integral with nonzero residue. Assume each level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, indexed by a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and by $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq SL(2,\mathbb Z)$, pulls `R.integers` back to itself. Let $N$ be a finite set of places of $FSS$ over the residue field of $A$, a place being a proper valuation subring containing the base field whose value ring is a principal ideal ring. Assume: every element $\tau$ of the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms which preserves `R.integers` induces, via `R.resAut`, an automorphism of $FSS$ over the residue field of $A$ whose action on places preserves $N$; every place $Q \notin N$ is moved by the induced automorphism of some level automorphism preserving `R.integers`; there is a component chart $C$ for $A$, $\bar F$, $FSS$ with $C$.integers $=$ `R.integers` and residue map agreeing with that of $R$; the maximal ideals of the subring $\bigcap_{Q \notin N} Q$ of $FSS$ correspond bijectively to the places $Q \notin N$, the ideal attached to $Q$ consisting of the $g$ with $g = 0$ or $\operatorname{ord}_Q g > 0$; and every $g \in FSS$ integral at all places off $N$ is the residue of some $f \in C$.integers which at each place $P$ in $C.\mathrm{dom}$ is integral with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$. Then for every place $Q \notin N$ there are $\zeta$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $f$ with $f$ and $\tau f$ both in $C$.integers, where $\tau =$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, such that $f$ is integral with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$ at every $P \in C.\mathrm{dom}$, while $\operatorname{ord}_Q$ of the residue of $f$ is positive and $\operatorname{ord}_Q$ of the residue of $\tau f$ is not positive.
--
--   This is the transport step which converts freeness of the level-automorphism action on the places off the node set into an explicit chart function that vanishes at a prescribed place $Q$ but not at its translate. It feeds the constructions of the local affinoid with node annuli on the supersingular chart at full level, in the three declarations that cite it.
